meta {
  name: Sync news feed blogposts
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/news-feed/blogposts
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-xtm-hub-token: {{xtm-hub-token}}
}

docs {
  Webhook called by n8n each time a blog post is published, edited or unpublished. It is only a trigger: the request
  body is ignored, the Hub fetches the latest blog posts itself and reconciles the news feed.

  Ensure xtm-hub-token is defined in environment. It is the system token: the sync runs as the system user.

  Answers:
  - 200 once the synchronization is committed, with the counts only:
    { "created": 1, "updated": 0, "dropped": 1, "provisionedPlatforms": 12 }
  - 401, with no body, when the token is missing or wrong (identical in both cases)
  - 429 when the rate limit is exceeded (30 requests per minute per IP)
  - 500 with { "message": "Unable to synchronize blog posts" } when anything fails, nothing is applied then.
    The details are in the Hub logs.
}
